"title": "Reflecting On 2024's 'Year Of Embodied AI': Hype And Reality", "content": "# Reflecting On 2024's 'Year Of 
Embodied AI': Hype And Reality. As the year of ChatGPT—2023—came to a close, there was a feeling in the air that 
something even bigger was coming in 2024. With one week until the new year, Brett Adcock of Figure AI Robotics 
proclaimed what many were hoping: that 2024 would be the “year of embodied AI.”. Just a few days later, the *New York 
Times* (paywall) claimed that “AI will supercharge robots” in 2024. This was quickly followed by the humanoid robotics 
company 1X announcing a $100 million fundraising round. Soon after, Figure AI raised the bar with a round of $675 
million. To many, it seemed inevitable that robots would soon unlock the same emergent capabilities observed in LLMs. 
