(0)0](#comments-4510816)\n\n© Reuters.\n\nInvesting.com -- Brazil’s Agriculture Minister Andre de Paula said the 
country’s 2026/27 agricultural Safra Plan will reach between 608 billion and 610 billion reais, equivalent to $117.53 
billion to $117.91 billion, according to newspaper Estadao on Monday.\n\nThe plan allocates a record 525.1 billion reais
in financing for medium and large-scale farmers, Estadao reported.\n\nThe total funding falls below what the 
